    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **275 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\nI implemented the per-city owner cap by following the project's existing daily-limit pattern:\n\n- **`EnsureCityOwnerLimit`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step that counts existing owners in the new owner's city (case-insensitive, excluding self) and throws `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` when the count already reached the cap of 8.\n- **`CityOwnerLimitExceededException`** \u2014 a checked exception.\n- **`CityOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds **400 Bad Request** with a `ProblemDetail`.\n- Wired `ensureCityLimit` into `owners.POST.yml` right after `normalizeCity`, so the check runs against the canonical city spelling and shares the same `transaction` governance as the rest of the pipeline.\n\nThe existing `Cp14Tests` (create 8 owners in a fresh city, expect the 9th to be rejected with 400) passes, and no other tests regressed.",
